From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:02:39 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: aop_audio: Drive the T8140 AOP audio services

The T8140 (MacBook Neo) had its own AOP audio module next to aop_audio,
both bound to services of the same AOP. Make it one driver: aop_audio
matches apple,t8140-aop-audio as well, and the compatible's match data
selects what the probe sets up. The PDM microphone setups of T8103 to
T6041 keep their hardware configuration as before, and T8140 gets the
services it already had, now as the aop_t8140 backend of the same
module.

The T8140 code moves unchanged apart from its probe and unbind, which
the shared platform driver calls. Its card keeps the t8140-aop-audio
driver name, its id and names, PCMs and controls, so UCM and userspace
see the same card. Module autoloading follows the compatible, so DTs
need no change. The module is snd-soc-aop for every machine now.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5d99c282f87b240cf8572e2a913e3139e92d70d8)
[dylan: Took the upstream change. Kept omacom's 7.2 forms in context:
 the four-argument of_device_table!() with MODULE_OF_TABLE, and the
 mt7932-*.py MAINTAINERS pattern. The rest of the T8140 backend matches
 5d99c282f apart from the omacom 7.2 THIS_MODULE and
 snd_soc_register_component calls already in the tree.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
[dylan: tier d: aop_t8140 is a submodule of aop_audio, and module!()
 defines THIS_MODULE only at the crate root, so name it crate::THIS_MODULE
 (the tip's this_module::<crate::LocalModule>() is not in omacom 7.2).]
